{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429937-totem-advantages-questions","id":429937,"title":"Totem Advantages Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T01:46:31-08:00","id":429937,"title":"Totem Advantages Questions","content":"So, looking over Totem creation rules, and I have some questions.<br /> <br /> <b>Are the Advantage(s) granted by a Totem limited to +1 Dot?</b> All of the examples seem to imply yes, but there's nothing explicitly stated. If multiple dots are allowed, does that mean the totem can bring a WW or Wolf-Blooded to 7 or higher? If multiple dots are allowed and traits can not exceed 6 (or PU+1, whichever is higher), what happens?<br /> <br /> <b>Do people gaining a merit as an Advantage need to meet the prerequisites?</b> If yes, and they don't qualify, what happens? If no, how does this work for Merits that simply make no sense for that individual pack member? Anchored for a human character, for instance. If no, does this include granting Supernatural merits to werewolves?<br /> <br /> <b>Can &quot;Totem&quot; merit and &quot;Dedicated Locus&quot; merit be granted by the Totem Merit?</b> As a related question, can a Pack have more than one dedicated locus.<br /> <br /> <b>Do all choices regarding a Merit need to be the same?</b> If a Totem grants Allies or Professional Training, do all choices (subject of the Allies, type and Asset Skills of Professional Training and granted benefits) have to be the same?<br /> <br /> <b>Can Retainers be pack members?</b> If yes, do they gain the Advantages of a totem? If yes, what happens when you select &quot;Retainer&quot; as one of your Totem advantages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T04:26:14-08:00","id":430013,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on your (very good) queries. Note that I didn't write the totem bit of the rules though so these are opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429937-totem-advantages-questions#post429937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, looking over Totem creation rules, and I have some questions.<br /> <br /> <b>Are the Advantage(s) granted by a Totem limited to +1 Dot?</b> All of the examples seem to imply yes, but there's nothing explicitly stated. If multiple dots are allowed, does that mean the totem can bring a WW or Wolf-Blooded to 7 or higher? If multiple dots are allowed and traits can not exceed 6 (or PU+1, whichever is higher), what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure whether they are just limited to +1, this will need clarification. Worth popping it into the Errata thread. I would <i>personally</i> say it should be capped at +1 for sanity's sake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do people gaining a merit as an Advantage need to meet the prerequisites?</b> If yes, and they don't qualify, what happens? If no, how does this work for Merits that simply make no sense for that individual pack member? Anchored for a human character, for instance. If no, does this include granting Supernatural merits to werewolves? </div> </div> </div>All good points that need clarification. My thoughts:<br /> - People don't need to meet the prereqs.<br /> - For merits that make no sense, use the same set-up as if it were a merit they already had, choose another relevant merit.<br /> - I would say no Supernatural merits from the GMC book for werewolves in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can &quot;Totem&quot; merit and &quot;Dedicated Locus&quot; merit be granted by the Totem Merit?</b> As a related question, can a Pack have more than one dedicated locus. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think Totem probably needs to be explicitly stated as something you can't take from the Totem's advantage to stop a recursive situation :P<br /> <br /> I believe a pack can have more than one dedicated locus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do all choices regarding a Merit need to be the same?</b> If a Totem grants Allies or Professional Training, do all choices (subject of the Allies, type and Asset Skills of Professional Training and granted benefits) have to be the same? </div> </div> </div>Whatever trait is bought, everyone gets the same thing, so I would assume that's true of the details of the trait (the subject of the Allies, etc).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can Retainers be pack members?</b> If yes, do they gain the Advantages of a totem? If yes, what happens when you select &quot;Retainer&quot; as one of your Totem advantages? </div> </div> </div>For this, I'd point to the text of the Retainer merit: &quot;Her retainer isn\u2019t part of the pack; their relationship is strictly one-to-one.&quot; If they join the pack, they are no longer your Retainer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T04:43:14-08:00","id":430022,"title":"","content":"I can only answer based on my reading and understanding of it, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Are the Advantage(s) granted by a Totem limited to +1 Dot?</b> </div> </div> </div>The text isn't clear (and I'd flag this up as errata if I were you), but I note the phrasing &quot;The players buy <b>a</b> benefit&quot; (my formatting). My reading of that would be you can buy a single merit, a single skill speciality, a single dot of a skill, a single dot of an attribute, etc. Just on my gut I'd say that merits with a variable cost can be bought at more than 1 dot if applicable (and 1 dot of Allies represents something very different to 5 dots of Allies), but a dev should probably rule on that. So you couldn't buy 2 dots of Strength, but you could buy 1 dot of Strength and 1 dot of Dexterity, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do people gaining a merit as an Advantage need to meet the prerequisites?</b> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be that they do, but that if you don't meet the prereqs you get something similar and suitable (like you do if you already have the merit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can &quot;Totem&quot; merit and &quot;Dedicated Locus&quot; merit be granted by the Totem Merit?</b> </div> </div> </div>&quot;These Merits are specific to Uratha, without Storyteller approval otherwise.&quot; I would take this to read that neither merit could be taken by the Totem (and nor could Anchored, Moon-kissed or any other merit from the general werewolf merits or werewolf fighting merits) as they are not Uratha. My reading of the Totem rules is that the Totem is in effect taking the merit, and then passing the benefit to the pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do all choices regarding a Merit need to be the same?</b> </div> </div> </div>Allies (Monocle Wearers) and Allies (Dank Meme Creators) are functionally two different merits. Yes, all choices must be the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can Retainers be pack members?</b> </div> </div> </div>Don't see why they couldn't be, but Retainers provided by the Totem (and I'd be wary of letting that happen anyway without good rationale) I would not count as members of the pack. Personally-purchased retainers could easily represent wolf-blooded and associated humans though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I hope this helps. As I've said, I can't offer definite answers, but this is my impression from a thorough read.<br /> <br /> *edit* Sniped by a dev. Sad times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:36:29-07:00","id":438235,"title":"","content":"Just bumping this thread with a question of my own.<br /> <br /> It is said in the Totem Creation section at the least that all members gain the benefit from the Totem whether or not they invest Dot's in the Totem merit or not, so one could have a member with no dot's in the Background and who happily ignores the Spirits Ban, all it can do is take away Totem Merit dots apparently, and still benefits from the traits the Totem brings to the Pack.<br /> <br /> Is this correct understanding on my part?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:50:16-07:00","id":438242,"title":"","content":"I think that might be a throwback to a time where dots = bennies. Might be better if breaking it takes away benefits but leaves dots alone, since they're more of a chargen thing than something that matters in-play now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}